From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bmle69 <128874520+bmle69@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 23:26:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Older devices: decode BC textures across the CPU's cores

With tex_bc_cpu, pkg_upload_ decoded each BC texture on the submit thread, one block at a time, so
a level load that brings many textures in one frame stalled that frame: on an iPhone 13 Pro (A15),
Super Mario Bros. Wonder's World 1-1 loaded 86 textures, 67.6 MB, in 132.6 ms of a 160 ms frame.

nvn_bc_decode_par splits a region's block rows into bands (at least 16 block rows, at most 4 bands
per core, at most 16 cores counted) and decodes them with dispatch_apply. Regions under 256x256
pixels stay on the calling thread. Each band is whole block rows, so its offsets are those of its
first row and only the last band can end in a partial block row, which nvn_bc_decode trims as before.
The bands write disjoint rows and share no mutable state, so the output is byte for byte that of
nvn_bc_decode. The buffer-to-texture copy path (patch 0063) uses it too.

t_bcdec checks the equality for the BC1 to BC5 formats and BC6H unsigned, with both BC6H outputs,
at 9 sizes on both sides of the threshold, odd widths and heights, a padded destination pitch and a
guard after the last row. t_bc_cpu uploads two textures large enough to take the multi-core path.

Measured by the author: on a Mac, BC7 2048x2048 19.8 ms -> 2.7 ms, BC3 6.1 -> 0.8 ms. On the A15,
the largest load frame went from 67.6 MB in 132.6 ms to 60.7 MB in 76.6 ms (the deswizzle before it
is still single-threaded). GPUs with BC support never reach this path.

Upstream-Status: fork-only (extends the fork-only CPU BC decode, declined seedds/nxnative#488)
Reason: speeds up bc-cpu-decode, which upstream declined, and runs only with tex_bc_cpu on a GPU without BC support
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#777
